      "writtenOn": "2023-03-28T16:17:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you want to save the cost of image comparisons after you make equals() work accurately, consider making this just detect null -\u003e something and something -\u003e null changes, i.e.\n\n```\n// Actual image comparisons have shown to be very expensive. Since it\u0027s rare that\n// an application changes the cover artwork between multiple images once it\u0027s not \n// null anymore, we just look for changes between \"something\" and \"nothing.\" Use\n// .equals() in the future if you want this behavior to change. It will compare\n// the underlying bitmaps.\nif (image !\u003d null \u0026\u0026 m.image !\u003d null || image \u003d\u003d null \u0026\u0026 m.image \u003d\u003d null) {\n    return true;\n}\n```",
